			{
				"type": "Comment",
				"start": 0,
				"end": 412,
				"data": "\n\tThe deferred separator in front of a run-ending sibling — a comment, a {@debug} — is that\n\tfollower's own per-width wrap, exactly as before an element: when the element overflows and\n\tgoes block-style, the content line is only 97 wide, so the follower stays on it. Prettier\n\tbreaks that space with the container instead. The width boundary of the hug itself is in\n\tinline_sibling_space_before_bounding.\n"
			},
			{
				"type": "Text",
				"start": 412,
				"end": 414,
